{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01PJEiuJUbJ7HTkBKkXvRppY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Skill Foundry â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-runnable) â€” Session Summary\n\nGrounded bullet claims, sourced from `planning/portfolio-program/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (the member document).\n\n## Scope & framing\n- **This plan is Phase 0 only** â€” the shared infrastructure every skill cycle reuses; it builds the substrate, not the skills themselves.\n- **Cognitive skills are out of scope here.** Gandalf, Ramanujan, lit-review, data-analysis, ML-code, and code-verification â€” plus the recreate-a-paper proof and the NS1 demo â€” are each their *own* researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle (per `crucible/PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`), not waves in this plan.\n- **Program North Star (LOCKED):** a deep, self-improving skill repository where every skill carries a LOCKED North Star, journals its real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\" sessions *without drifting*. First proof (a later cycle): a recreate-a-paper recipe reproducing the Gelman ANOVA paper, graded on architecture/handoff success.\n- **Frozen design:** `crucible/MASTER-PLAN.md` (v4) â€” 6 contiguous, TAP-gated waves. The **orchestrator (not a sub-agent) runs the ground-truth gate** after each wave. test-command: `node --test test/`.\n\n## Trust model (EXECUTE/GATE, \"FIX-16â€²\")\n- **Foreman discards sub-agent transcripts** and records no transcript/session id or artifact hash â€” so the gate does *not* try to prove \"an LLM genuinely ran.\"\n- Guarantees rest on **two forgery-resistant artifacts the orchestrator owns:** (a) the **gate artifact** (TAP result of `node --test`, run by the orchestrator) and (b) the **post-execute test-file content-hash baseline** (a sub-agent can't later alter the tests it's graded by).\n- **LLM-judge / cross-family judging is ADVISORY only** (isolated per FIX-15), never part of the gate command (PRINCIPLE-D). LLM build work lives in EXECUTE; the deterministic GATE verifies structure + runs deterministic tests.\n- Build root = the portfolio-program folder (a Node project); templates + canary SETS are written into `../../skills/` so **Skill Foundry stays stateless prose** (canaries are data/refs).\n\n## The 6 waves (each done-when `node --test test/` is GREEN)\n- **Wave 1 â€” Eval-harness go/no-go spike + test bootstrap:** prove a wrapped validator emits real TAP `ok N` events the gate counts, a prose-deliverable coverage path passes the vacuous-green guard, and an *unreachable advisory host* still leaves the gate GREEN. NO-GO fallback recorded: validators run as a standalone Node process via `test-command`.\n- **Wave 2 â€” Three validators as TAP emitters:** one harness exposing (i) schema+path-existence, (ii) deterministic canary eval (byte-identical TAP on repeat runs), (iii) numeric-tolerance grader calling a pure offline reference fn â€” with the advisory cross-family judge isolated so its exit/stdout never reach the gate.\n- **Wave 3 â€” Machine-checkable handoff-contract gate:** gates a stage handoff on schema-valid + all `artifact_refs` resolve on disk + `north_star` round-trips byte-identical + `open_questions` empty; wired into Anchor's HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md and Crucible's locate-plan path.\n- **Wave 4 â€” Skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model swap:** per-skill repo skeleton (NORTH-STAR.md with non-goals as negative tests, SKILL.md, references/, LESSONS.md, journal/, CHANGELOG.md) + a logical-tierâ†’model config table; a swap test proves changing the table changes the resolved model with **zero skill-prose edits**. Note: the swap test pins a model-respecting backend (gemini-cli driver) because the default Claude backend ignores `opts.model` (else the test passes vacuously).\n- **Wave 5 â€” Journal 7-field schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop:** sleep meta-recipe (cluster â†’ cross-context-corroborated distill â†’ North-Star gate â†’ eval gate â†’ versioned promote with git rollback), TAP-tested on **fixture** journals (real skills don't exist yet). Lessons advancing a non-goal are REJECTED; canary regressions block promotion (rollback); same-context-only corroboration is not shipped (R5).\n- **Wave 6 â€” Governance wiring + canary versioning + citation hygiene:** `map.json` records canary SETS + templates as data/refs; drift checker + foundry invariant pytest stay GREEN; canary sets are versioned append-only (deletion = human call); **SkillsBenchâ†’2602.12670 corrected and MemoryGraft dropped** in carried docs.\n\n## Definition of done\n- **DONE = Wave 6 GREEN** (orchestrator-run `node --test test/`). At that point the shared substrate exists and is proven on fixtures: deterministic eval harness (3 validators), machine-checkable handoff contract, per-skill repo templates + swappable tierâ†’model seam, journal schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop with rollback, and Foundry governance wiring.\n- **The cognitive-skill cycles, the recreate-a-paper proof, and the NS1 demonstration build ON this substrate next** â€” each as its own researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle.\n\n---\n\nNote: `report.md` in the repo root is a *different* artifact â€” a researchPrime study on Foreman parallelism (grass-4199), not part of this implementation-plan trio session. Want me to fold that in, or keep this summary scoped to the implementation plan only?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3763,"cache_read_input_tokens":35355,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3763},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b636aa25-0bba-40ef-8a1b-b4cbf6b3840f","uuid":"74af4252-2898-4cae-b085-acd9249229aa","request_id":"req_011CcKGjJmmwLvJdzmFBjGzs"}
